title: Linux Bubblewrap Lifecycle and Limits
status: implemented
created: 2026-10-31
author: adrian
context: "The isolation spike proved the bwrap view but left two gaps: the sandbox shares the caller's session unless --new-session is set, and it has no resource controls. Evidence on NixOS, kernel 7.2.12, systemd user manager, cgroup v2: systemd-run --user --scope starts the harness; systemctl --user freeze and thaw stop and resume the workload; MemoryMax=64M and TasksMax=16 bound a 256 MiB allocation and a 64-thread hog. The copied lifecycle.sh is the isolation ADR's tested process-group path. A host without a usable user manager selects the fallback by checking systemctl --user show-environment; with XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/nonexistent the launcher exits 69 and lifecycle.sh freezes, resumes and kills. Launcher cost: direct 23.8ms median, scope 47.5ms median. CPUQuota was not applied or tested."
problem: "The isolation harness cannot create a separate session without losing group-based lifecycle control, and it cannot bound memory or task count. We need a lifecycle design that uses cgroups where available and falls back explicitly where they are not."
goals[5]:
  - Run the sandbox in its own session by default
  - Freeze and resume the sandbox through cgroup v2
  - Apply per-sandbox memory and task limits
  - Fall back to process-group signalling without systemd
  - Reuse the existing harness and argv builder unchanged
nonGoals[4]:
  - Nix devShell activation or the environment allowlist
  - Egress proxy or port forwarding
  - macOS confinement
  - A long-lived supervisor or daemon
requirements[6]{id,title,slug,description}:
  FR-001,"Session By Default",session-by-default,"The harness runs with --new-session and lifecycle control moves to the cgroup."
  FR-002,"Cgroup Freeze",cgroup-freeze,"A transient systemd user scope freezes and thaws the sandbox through systemctl --user freeze and thaw."
  FR-003,"Resource Limits",resource-limits,"The scope applies MemoryMax and TasksMax, and a workload exceeding either fails rather than consuming the host."
  FR-004,"Process Group Fallback",process-group-fallback,"Without a usable user manager the copied lifecycle.sh runs the sandbox and uses process-group signals."
  FR-005,"Shared Code",shared-code,"The isolation harness and argv builder are copied unchanged; only launchers and scripts differ."
  FR-006,"Tests",tests,"A freeze test, a memory-limit test and a task-limit test run from one command; the fallback script is the isolation ADR's tested path."
nonFunctional[3]{id,title,slug,description}:
  NFR-001,"Systemd Optional",systemd-optional,"Systemd is detected at runtime through systemctl --user show-environment; its absence selects the fallback."
  NFR-002,"No Supervisor",no-supervisor,"The scope is transient and owned by systemd; the harness gains no daemon."
  NFR-003,"Cost Recorded",cost-recorded,"The systemd launcher's startup cost is measured and recorded beside the isolation cost."
acceptance[6]{id,title,slug,description}:
  AC-001,"New Session",new-session,"The sandboxed command runs in its own session under the scope."
  AC-002,"Freeze And Thaw",freeze-and-resume,"Freezing the scope stops the workload making progress; thawing resumes it."
  AC-003,"Memory Limit",memory-limit,"A workload exceeding MemoryMax fails instead of consuming host memory."
  AC-004,"Task Limit",task-limit,"A workload exceeding TasksMax fails instead of spawning without bound."
  AC-005,"Fallback Script",fallback,"The copied lifecycle.sh performs freeze, resume and kill through process groups, as recorded in the isolation ADR."
  AC-006,"Cost Recorded",cost-recorded,"The launcher's startup cost is measured and recorded."
edgeCases[3]{id,title,slug,description}:
  EC-001,"Systemd Absent",systemd-absent,"The launcher detects the missing user manager and selects the fallback; exercised with XDG_RUNTIME_DIR=/nonexistent."
  EC-002,"Delegation Absent",delegation-absent,"A user manager without cgroup delegation is not detected up front: the scope start fails and the probe exits non-zero, leaving the tested process-group fallback to be selected by the caller. Accepted as an unverified host state."
  EC-003,"Scope Name Collision",scope-name-collision,"Transient scope names include the pid and are collected on exit."
